), (1,4,5), (2,2,4), (2,4,10), (1,9,10), and (2,5,9). SSS therefore gives eight congruence classes.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2009_AMC_8_Q20","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":[],"id":"side-length-signatures","label":"Classify by side lengths","methodDirectNodeIds":{"side-length-signatures":["cnm_174","cnm_122"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_174","cnm_122"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_110","cnm_121"],"id":"horizontal-base-classification","label":"Classify by the horizontal base","methodDirectNodeIds":{"horizontal-base-classification":["cnm_120","math:symmetry-counting","cnm_p148","cnm_174","cnm_122"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_120","math:symmetry-counting","cnm_p148","cnm_174","cnm_122","cnm_110","cnm_121"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"90°","reason":"SSS gives △ABD≅△ACD, so ∠ADB=∠ADC. Since DB and DC are opposite rays, these equal angles sum to 180°, making each 90°.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_126_q4","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"id":"sss-and-linear-pair","label":"SSS and equal supplements","nodeIds":["cnm_122","cnm_121","cnm_062"]},{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_120"],"id":"solution:sss-and-linear-pair:df1b7662ed11","label":"SSS and equal supplementary angles","methodDirectNodeIds":{"sss-and-linear-pair":["cnm_122","cnm_121","cnm_062"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_122","cnm_121","cnm_062","cnm_120"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":3,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"3 cm","reason":"C'D'=CD and CD=3 cm, so C'D'=3 cm.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"cn-math","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"cnm_127_q2","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_120"],"id":"copied-segment","label":"Use the prescribed segment equality","methodDirectNodeIds":{"copied-segment":["cnm_055","cnm_127","cnm_